so  first question i have for you is even  after leading your own tv show was there  anything about headlining a  gigantic disney feature film that kind  of took you by surprise uh  yes a hundred percent i mean still  everything that happens to me regarding  you know  work and filming stuff like blows my  mind  it never feels real you know i i love  acting so much because of  you know the art of it you know and like  like connecting with people that you've  never even met through a screen  like that's always been what's drawn me  to  acting into this industry and so then  when  i haven't even really thought about it  and all of a sudden like it's my face on  a poster  or something like that it just like  completely blows my mind  um so yes a hundred percent i have those  what is my life moments pretty much  every day  um and it's it's really  crazy it's because you earned them and  deserve them  oh thank you so one of my absolute  favorite  parts of the movie is the snowflake  speech and this is a little bit of a  of a deep heavy question but with that  in mind  what is something about yourself that  maybe you once  viewed as a flaw or imperfection and  then  came to realize that's what made you  special yeah well i think  um honestly i connected with sam a lot  from the very beginning from the very  first time i read the script because  we both have this natural instinct to  want to do things ourselves and to be  super independent  and i think that characteristic  can be both good and bad you know it's  great to be independent  it's great to want to do things by  yourself but in a sense it sort of  distances you from other people  sometimes you know and when you're not  asking for help when you're not  um sort of pulling people into your life  into your life you can feel um alone  you know so i think that's definitely  something that i  see in myself that i see in sam um and  that  is both um a great strength and can feel  like a weakness  you know depending on how you use it on  how it sort of  um how it sort of comes out you know  um and sort of that journey of  figuring out how to use all these  characteristics you have and sort of  channel them into something positive  and getting all of the good things out  of them rather than the bad things  um or the not bad but more difficult  things um  and that's something that i've  definitely experienced and i think sam  has ex  same experiences throughout the movie um  so that's definitely something that i  would say is a  great strength and also um flaw if um  if sort of used in the wrong way or if  it if  it comes out in the wrong in the wrong  way i can certainly understand that  so yet another part of the movie that i  absolutely loved was just  the ensemble everybody is fantastic in  it so  i got a couple of questions pertaining  to the rest of the ensemble for you so  just tell me who who is the answer to  the question and maybe a little bit why  so first who would you say is the most  like their character in the movie  i would say the great thing about this  film is that everyone is so much like  their character  in a lot of ways you know um  like art really imitates life in that  sense and it really became very  apparent to me when i had met all of  them and then when they were playing  their characters because obviously  you know isabella um has a lot of  similarities to january and also some  not  and um and you know we we all do  i feel like tuma's strength is really  reflected  in niles and you know vice versa um  matteo and folly are a lot of alike in  that they're both very quirky  they're both very funny um olivia  and um roxanna i feel like i think  they're pretty similar  in that like they just have this great  big open heart  you know and and again i've sort of  explained to you how i'm similar to my  character  but yeah i wouldn't say there's one  person that's um more similar to their  characters than anyone else  um but i would say we all definitely  have a lot of similarities to our  characters which is what i think  makes sort of the acting and the whole  thing so um authentic  i'll squeeze in one more here if you  could swap roles with anyone in the  movie who would you pick and why  ooh i think i would have to pick skyler  who plays james  i think he's such a funny character like  the  the lines he has the things he says are  so funny  and also when he like duplicates himself  and he has like a bunch of him like i  feel like that would be really fun to  sort of like  pick a personality for each of the  different copies of yourself which he  kind of got to do which i which i  watched and was like  really impressed by and really i it  looked really fun to me so  probably his character kind of want him  to get a whole spin-off movie now so i  could see more of that  i mean secret society too  huge congratulations thanks so much for  your time today  of course really nice to meet you

